    "descriptions": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_ed125b877e1f",
            "level": {
              "value": 1
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "You bear a grudge, inherited from a blasphemous asura forebear in your bloodline, against a particular deity and their works. You also have some vestigial signs of your previous incarnation, such as a second set of shoulder blades without usable arms, a set of mostly closed eyes where no eyes belong, or strange scarring reminiscent of a mouth. You gain the Find Fault reaction.\n\n**Find Fault**\n\n- **Activate:** Reaction\n- **Traits:** concentrate\n- **Trigger:** You attempt a saving throw against a spell or magic effect but haven't rolled yet\n\nYou find some kind of fault with the magic, using that flaw to protect yourself from the effect. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your saving throw against the triggering effect, which increases to a +2 circumstance bonus if the effect is divine and originates from a worshipper of the deity you chose for your grudge."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
